# TennisConnect Design System

These rules define the visual identity of TennisConnect.

The goal is to maintain a clean, modern and premium user experience.

---

# Design Philosophy

Every screen should feel:

- Modern
- Premium
- Spacious
- Friendly
- Professional
- Sports-oriented

Avoid clutter.

Whitespace is part of the design.

---

# Inspiration

Preferred design references:

- Apple
- Airbnb
- Linear
- Notion
- Stripe

Avoid outdated dashboard styles.

---

# Visual Language

The interface should feel:

- Light
- Fresh
- Fast
- Elegant

Never over-design.

Less is more.

---

# Responsive Design

Always design for:

- Mobile
- Tablet
- Desktop

Mobile first.

Desktop should not simply be a stretched mobile layout.

Tablet requires its own layout adjustments.

---

# Layout

Prefer

max-w-6xl

or

max-w-7xl

for content.

Center major sections.

Use generous spacing.

Avoid full-width content unless necessary.

---

# Spacing

Use consistent spacing.

Prefer

gap-2

gap-3

gap-4

gap-6

gap-8

gap-10

gap-12

Avoid random spacing values.

Whitespace improves readability.

---

# Border Radius

Preferred

rounded-xl

rounded-2xl

rounded-3xl

Avoid mixing many different radius values.

---

# Shadows

Use soft shadows.

Examples

shadow-sm

shadow-md

shadow-lg

Avoid heavy shadows.

---

# Cards

Cards should be:

- rounded
- clean
- minimal
- slightly elevated

Hover:

- subtle shadow
- slight scale
- smooth transition

Avoid aggressive animations.

---

# Buttons

Buttons should be:

- rounded
- readable
- consistent

Primary button

Green

Secondary

Outline

Danger

Red only when necessary.

Avoid too many button styles.

---

# Colors

Primary accent

Lime Green

The green should feel like a tennis ball.

Use green only as an accent.

Avoid large green backgrounds.

Neutral colors should dominate.

---

# Typography

Readable.

Comfortable.

Large headings.

Good line spacing.

Avoid very long paragraphs.

Hierarchy

H1

H2

H3

Body

Caption

---

# Icons

Use Lucide icons.

Icons should:

- support the text
- not replace text unnecessarily

Keep icon sizes consistent.

Examples

w-4 h-4

w-5 h-5

w-6 h-6

---

# Images

Images should:

- have rounded corners when appropriate
- use object-cover
- maintain aspect ratio

Always provide fallback images.

---

# Avatars

Always circular.

Large enough to recognize.

Hover edit buttons should be subtle.

---

# Cover Images

Use gradient overlays.

Use dark overlay for readability.

Maintain consistent heights.

Desktop:

Large hero.

Mobile:

Reduced height.

---

# Forms

Inputs should be:

clean

minimal

easy to scan

Prefer

border-b

for profile editing.

Avoid heavy borders.

---

# Tables

Keep tables simple.

Readable.

Responsive.

Avoid excessive borders.

---

# Animations

Use Framer Motion only when it improves UX.

Animations should be:

Fast

Smooth

Natural

Avoid flashy animations.

---

# Hover Effects

Hover should be subtle.

Examples

scale-105

shadow-lg

background transition

Avoid large movement.

---

# Loading States

Always show:

Spinner

Skeleton

Placeholder

Avoid blank screens.

---

# Empty States

Every list should have:

Friendly message

Helpful action

Example

"No players found."

Provide next action when possible.

---

# Pagination

Use shared AppPagination component.

Center pagination.

Scroll to top after page change.

Hide pagination when only one page exists.

Responsive on mobile.

---

# Mobile

Touch targets should be comfortable.

Buttons should not be too small.

Avoid horizontal scrolling.

Stack content naturally.

---

# Tablet

Tablet is not desktop.

Adjust:

Typography

Spacing

Grid

Buttons

Specifically for medium screens.

---

# Desktop

Use available space wisely.

Do not stretch content too much.

Prefer centered layouts.

---

# Accessibility

Images require alt.

Buttons require labels.

Maintain sufficient color contrast.

Support keyboard navigation.

---

# UI Consistency

Player pages

Coach pages

Travel pages

Articles

Marketplace

Admin

should all share the same design language.

---

# AI Instructions

When generating UI:

Preserve the TennisConnect visual identity.

Reuse existing components before creating new ones.

Do not redesign existing pages unless requested.

Prefer consistency over creativity.

When multiple UI solutions exist:

Choose the one that best matches the existing TennisConnect style.

---

# Final Principle

Every new screen should look like it was designed by the same designer.

Consistency is more important than originality.
